decision: changes-requested

Three high-severity blockers remain:

- **N17 — Missing dependency leaves bypass symlink detection**, [validate_carry.go:125](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2791357838/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:125). With `b/link -> ../a` and `b.dependsOn=["b/link/input"]`, deleting `a/input` makes `Lstat` fail. The guard skips that dependency, and lexical selection misses `b`, carrying its stale pass.
- **N18 — Dependency case aliases escape invalidation**, [validate_carry.go:128](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2791357838/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:128). On case-insensitive Unix filesystems, `A/input` can identify `a/input`, while symlink resolution preserves the supplied spelling. Dependency comparison remains case-sensitive; the physical alias check covers module directories only. This conclusion follows from source inspection; that filesystem configuration was not exercised locally.
- **N19 — Duplicate check IDs can turn failure into success**, [validate_carry.go:142](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2791357838/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:142). Validation permits a default check and appended override with the same name. A failing entry followed by a passing entry shares one ID; the map retains only the pass, which carry then copies into both entries. This violates R4.

R5-N15 is fixed. R5-N16 is partial because missing leaves bypass its new guard.

Applied the review workflow and security, backend-Go, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Focused regression tests, focused `go vet`, and focused race tests passed. Full validation commands were started but had not completed; their sealed canonical evidence is cited below. Assessments could not run because the read-only sandbox denied scratch creation. The checkout remains unchanged, and no attestation was recorded.

